29,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The staffing situation is critical. The late-turn pool is exhausted, and we are relying heavily on overtime.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"The crowd counts are a lie. People complain about the platforms, but the real time-sink is the connection gaps.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"How fascinating. It seems our ""headline"" budget is merely a facade for a series of escalating contractor fees.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Servas,,"I have found that we often forget our own successes. We have tried these paths before, and some actually worked.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,It seems the physical ground is as unpredictable as the bureaucracy. Some plans may be far riskier than they appear.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, if the connection gaps are the issue, we cannot simply add more services if there are no crews to run them.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"Then we fix the schedule, not the platforms! We keep chasing ghosts because people shout the loudest about the crowds.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"While you argue over the ghosts, the ticketing contractors are quietly eating the paving budget. A most elegant tragedy.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Servas,,"Patience, my friends. When we align the human element with the lessons of the past, the solution reveals itself.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I wonder if the plans we are considering account for the ""unrecorded voids"" in the old shells.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Asuka,,I will not support any plan that assumes a magical increase in manpower. We must prioritize efficiency over expansion.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"Efficiency means cutting the dead time between trains. I'm not interested in ""manpower"" if the timing is still broken.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I shall be looking for the plan that doesn't hide its long-term liabilities in a footnote. Logic dictates we avoid the ""cheap"" option.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Servas,,Let us look for the plan that respects the rhythm of the city and the reality of our history.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I am concerned about the ""yes"" we cannot see. If the joint operators are not aligned, the plan will stall.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
